# Text files are checked out with LF line ends whatever core.autocrlf says (Git for Windows sets it to true), so that a
# clone builds the same files as the development tree: C# verbatim strings keep the line ends of the source (a CRLF
# checkout built another PortMobile.dll), and the phone's sh needs LF (host/vinput/hidctl.sh).
* text=auto eol=lf
# cmd.exe finds its labels reliably only in CRLF files.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.patch -text
